WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.402
-Very nice to have you here
in studio.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.937
We wanted to give you a taste of
what it's like

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.571
to be in an arena again.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:07.640
-Thank you. It feels good.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.741
-It feels good.
-I missed it.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.543
I missed it.
-You missed that.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.411
You had your first
preseason game.

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:13.813
You didn't play.
-Did not.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.081
-But you guys played against
the Lakers.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.549
So it's officially starting up
again.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.550
How are you feeling?

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.817
-I feel great.

00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:20.586
It was crazy to come out.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.656
We had fans during the playoffs,
but it still felt different.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.558
You know, like the benches
are all spread apart,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.993
our seats on the benches
were spread apart.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.994
Now they're just like --
Two months later they're like,

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:31.297
"Nah, okay, we'll just get
everybody back together.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.931
Let's sell those tickets
next to the bench."

00:00:32.931 --> 00:00:35.168
So it was just good to be out
there again, you know?

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:39.138
-As a veteran, how important is
preseason basketball to you?

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.941
-It's -- It's necessary.
-Okay.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.178
-But, you know, playing a game
that doesn't count is --

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.380
it's always a little weird,
but it's just nice to, like --

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.948
after doing training camp
and scrimmaging

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.817
against your teammates
the whole time,

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.485
it's nice to play against
other people.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:55.488
-You joined the Nets halfway
through last season.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.590
You had a chance then to sign
a contract anywhere.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.624
You chose to stay in New York.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:00:59.692
I know you spent
a lot of time here

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.427
and it's your first time
playing here.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.429
How have you enjoyed it so far?

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.231
-It was great, man.
It was nice to --

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.067
You know, I had that stint
last year

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.768
and really got to know
the organization.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.970
You never really know until you
actually spend time there,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.073
and top to bottom, everybody in
the organization is incredible,

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.909
from the owners down to the
players, the staff, everything.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.978
So that was the reason.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.814
Also, the fans here in New York
are unbelievable.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:23.883
So it was a no-brainer for me.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.854
-So it's kind of crazy the level
of talent and fame on this team.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:31.424
Kyrie, Durant, Harden, yourself.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.059
You're a vet,
as we've established,

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.794
but you were, you know,
new to this team.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.961
Do they haze you at all?

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:37.330
Is there any like,
"you're the new guy,"

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.032
or do they kind of --
do you have the respect that

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.633
comes with being someone who's
been a multi-time All-Star?

00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:43.602
-No, since it was like --

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:45.371
I've been in the NBA
for 12 years now.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.172
I actually got to skip
the hazing part.

00:01:47.172 --> 00:01:49.341
We keep that for the rookies.
But it's light. It's fun.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:52.011
It's like carry
a Dora the Explorer backpack.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.446
That's what I had to do.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.747
-When you were a rookie
you had to carry

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.082
a Dora the Explorer backpack?
-Everywhere we went,

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.718
I carried a pink
Dora the Explorer backpack

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:02.121
into the arena,
hotels, everywhere.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.923
So that's the type of stuff
we do.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.792
-I would imagine --
I'm surprised there was one

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:08.461
that would even fit
on your back.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.462
-Well, you undo the strap
all the way.

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:11.497
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:13.032
-And you throw it on
one shoulder,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.101
and I would always just put
one shoe in there.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.368
-Alright. Gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:19.772
I imagine that's about all
you could fit.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.876
One thing I also want to ask
about being a 12-year vet,

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:26.011
is you get to know the referees.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:28.614
And you sort of have
a reputation for someone

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:31.483
who's going to talk
a little trash to the refs.

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:33.786
But there are times we've seen
you actually laugh at

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:34.954
what a ref has said back to you.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.089
What's happening
in those moments?

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:41.327
-My relationship with the refs
has -- It's been a rocky one.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.597
A few years back
I had a camp for kids,

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.999
and I had to ref
one of the kids' games.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:48.368
And I was doing so bad

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.203
that even the 7-year-olds
were yelling at me.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:54.307
And that's when I realized
I should be easier on the refs.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.776
Now, it's just like, I play
kind of two games a night,

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.077
where I'm playing basketball

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.613
but I'm also trying to make
the meanest ref laugh.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:04.683
So I'm just working out
ref-based puns before the game.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:09.087
You know, watching film
but also going over some jokes.

00:03:09.087 --> 00:03:10.923
But it's -- I don't know.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:13.392
They have such a hard job.
Such a hard job.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.828
No matter what,
somebody is going to hate you.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.097
Half of the audience
is going to hate you.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:22.935
-Yeah, and I would imagine, too,
again, having to basically

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:27.506
police people
who are beloved and famous

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:30.076
is a really tough job to have.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:34.013
-It can't be easy, and the best
ones are the ones who are like,

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.615
if they mess up, they're like,
"I messed up that one."

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.851
Because it's all happening
so fast,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.686
and they're just trying
their best,

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:44.223
and if any of you refs
are watching, I'm so sorry.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.425
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:50.496
I will try to do better this
season, but we all mess up.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:54.934
-I like that you -- you realized
that reffing a camp

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:58.337
because I went -- after I left,
I went and I hosted "SNL,"

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:00.472
and hosting "SNL,"
I immediately had --

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:02.408
I felt like I wanted to go back
to all of the hosts

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.844
that I had worked with over
the years and apologize to them

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.880
because anytime a host didn't
want to do something

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.850
that we wrote for them,
I thought, "You don't know."

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.285
And then I want back and I'm
like, "Oh, no, they knew."

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:14.654
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.590
Yeah, that's basically
my relationship

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.659
with the refs in a nutshell.
-You guys get to tip off

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.560
against the Bucks,
the world champs.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.728
Does it make it
a little more exciting?

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:23.830
I mean, obviously
it's a long season,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.598
and you can't get
too high or low,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.300
I would imagine,
for specific games.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.069
But does opening night have
an extra element of excitement

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.804
when you do something like that?

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.172
-Yeah, it is.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.740
Opening night is always just fun

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.142
just because it's the start
of a new season.

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:38.177
You don't know where you're
going to go.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.779
Also, playing
the defending champions,

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.881
it kind of sucks
'cause you have to sit there

00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:45.317
and watch them get their rings.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:50.289
So there's that aspect,
but they deserved it.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:51.624
Grueling season last season

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.827
and came out on top,
so it'll be fun.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.429
-I mean, you mentioned everybody
being back.

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.564
Does it seems like,
for the first time in two years,

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.332
"Oh, this is going to be
the kind of basketball season

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.968
that I was used to
before the pandemic hit"?

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.203
-I hope so. Yeah.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.706
I mean, the playoffs
felt pretty normal.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.441
But like I said,
there were still a few things.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:12.444
Like last night's game in L.A.
felt very normal,

00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:13.846
besides being a preseason game.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.581
So hopefully we're back

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:19.052
and people get vaccinated
and come to games.

